Ladybird’s CoreLocation provider now keeps a request waiting while
the authorization is still “not determined”. All three engines do
the same: Chromium’s LocationManagerDelegate returns early from
didChangeAuthorizationStatus: for kCLAuthorizationStatusNotDetermined
(location_manager_delegate.mm), WebKit’s CoreLocationGeolocationProvider
asks for authorization again and keeps waiting
(locationManagerDidChangeAuthorization:), and Gecko’s
CoreLocationLocationProvider only logs the change. None of them fails a
request until the authorization is denied or restricted.
